# ─── Server ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
PORT=8080

# Anything other than "production" behaves as development.
NODE_ENV=development

# ─── Auth (required) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Sign-up is open in development and closed in production unless this says
# otherwise. Keep it closed while SANDBOX_PROVIDER=host: a prompt is untrusted
# input and the host sandbox is a scoped working directory, not isolation.
# Create accounts with `node scripts/create-user.mjs <email> <password>`.
# ALLOW_REGISTRATION=false
JWT_SECRET="your_jwt_secret_here"
JWT_REFRESH="your_jwt_refresh_secret_here"
SALT_ROUNDS=10

# ─── The agent (required — this is the product) ───────────────────────────
# Which coding CLI the harness drives. This decides what endpoints work.
#
# codex (default) speaks the OpenAI API and takes an explicit compatible base
# url, so it runs on any aggregator — and therefore on any model that
# aggregator serves, Anthropic's included. It reads LLM_API_KEY and
# LLM_BASE_URL below, so one key covers the agent and the prompt helpers.
#
# claude-code speaks the Anthropic Messages API and needs ANTHROPIC_API_KEY or
# an ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL that implements it. An OpenAI-compatible endpoint will
# not do: the CLI gets a response it classifies as `unknown`, retries ten
# times with backoff, and the turn never produces a token.
# AGENT_HARNESS=claude-code
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY="sk-ant-..."
# ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL="http://127.0.0.1:8317"
# ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN="whatever_the_proxy_expects"
#
# Either way the harness installs its CLI itself on first use, so the host
# needs `pnpm` on PATH and network access to the npm registry. On a container
# with an ephemeral /tmp this happens every restart.

# ─── Sandbox: where the agent's files live and its shell runs ─────────────
# host   (default) — the backend's own disk. Zero setup, and the preview is a
#          local dev server. NOT isolation: the agent runs bash with this
#          process's privileges, so only use it where every user is trusted.
# vercel — a real remote microVM per session, seeded straight from
#          TEMPLATE_REPO by git clone. Required for anything multi-tenant.
# SANDBOX_PROVIDER=vercel
# VERCEL_PROJECT_ID="prj_..."
# VERCEL_TEAM_ID="team_..."
#
# Credentials: the SDK tries an OIDC token first and only then an explicit
# token — a logged-in Vercel CLI is NOT enough on its own. Either
#   local:      vercel link && vercel env pull   (writes VERCEL_OIDC_TOKEN
#               into .env.local; it is short-lived, so re-pull as needed)
#   deployed:   VERCEL_TOKEN="..."               (long-lived access token)
# VERCEL_TOKEN="..."
#
# One named sandbox per project, `persistent` so Vercel snapshots the
# filesystem on stop and restores it on resume — no state is serialised by
# hand. Vercel has no idle setting, only a wall-clock deadline, so every turn
# extends it; that is what makes SANDBOX_IDLE_MS behave as an idle timeout.
# Billing is metered on active CPU, provisioned memory (wall-clock while the
# sandbox is up), creations, transfer, and snapshot storage.
# SANDBOX_IDLE_MS=600000       # stop after this long with no activity
# SANDBOX_VCPUS=2              # 2048 MB memory per vCPU

# ─── Models (required) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Any OpenAI-compatible endpoint. Drives the codex agent, the "Enhance"
# button, project auto-naming, and chats with no project.
# Defaults to OpenRouter when unset.
# LLM_BASE_URL="https://openrouter.ai/api/v1"
LLM_API_KEY="your_openrouter_api_key_here"
# Comma separated; the first is the default unless LLM_DEFAULT_MODEL says so.
# Ids must match what the endpoint serves.
LLM_MODELS="anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.5,openai/gpt-4o-mini"
# LLM_DEFAULT_MODEL="anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.5"

# ─── Database ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Unset or non-postgres -> SQLite under .codefox/data, zero setup.
# DATABASE_URL="postgresql://username:password@localhost:5432/codefox"
#
# This repo carries no migrations, so a production database starts empty and
# every query fails. Set this to true for the first production boot to create
# the schema, then remove it — synchronize will drop a column to match an
# entity.
# DB_SYNCHRONIZE=true

# ─── Object storage (optional) ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Without these, uploads are written to .codefox/media on local disk.
# S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID="your_s3_access_key_id"
# S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY="your_s3_secret_access_key"
# S3_REGION="auto"
# S3_BUCKET_NAME="your_bucket_name"
# S3_ENDPOINT="https://<account_id>.r2.cloudflarestorage.com"
# S3_ACCOUNT_ID="your_cloudflare_account_id"
# S3_PUBLIC_URL="https://pub-xxx.r2.dev"

# ─── Email (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# With this false, registration confirms accounts immediately.
MAIL_ENABLED=false
# MAIL_HOST=smtp.example.com
# MAIL_USER=user@example.com
# MAIL_PASSWORD=topsecret
# MAIL_FROM=noreply@example.com
# MAIL_PORT=587
# MAIL_DOMAIN=your_net

# ─── Google OAuth (optional) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# The sign-in and sign-up modals hide the Google button unless the frontend
# also sets NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_OAUTH_ENABLED.
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=YOUR_CLIENT_ID
# GOOGLE_SECRET=Your_SECRET
# GOOGLE_CALLBACK_URL=http://localhost:8080/auth/google/callback

# ─── GitHub ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Currently disabled: GitHubModule is commented out in app.module.ts, so none
# of these are read. Left here for when it comes back.
